#! glm-dflash-taps-tp.patch — DFlash2 reads complete prompt taps at TP>1
#! (the round-131 port of upstream #1623).
#! The defect: with TF_GLM_PREFILL_REDUCE=split (the default), the DFlash2 tap
#! after layers 5/14/24/33/42 reads the rank's own residual for the other
#! ranks' rows — HALF the drafter's prompt context is stale at TP=2. Replies
#! never change (the verify accepts only the target's tokens); what suffers is
#! DRAFT ACCEPTANCE — our decode front. The fix: each rank taps its own rows
#! of a split piece (tapPieces), then shareTaps hands the tap rows to every
#! rank via the same relay that shares normed. Upstream's receipt (3x GB10,
#! TP=3, our checkpoint family EXL3-4bpw @ 078455ffe): +1.0-2.1% aggregate
#! decode at every level, the acceptance tokens/chunk up (2.37->2.42 chat,
#! 3.05->3.08 code), replies unchanged, TTFT cost none. Our own knobs sweep
#! confirms the effect's size: PREFILL_REDUCE=gather (complete taps, no split
#! glue) measured solo 46.2 vs the baseline 45.1 (+2.4%) — this patch delivers
#! that gain WITHOUT gather's prefill regression.
#! Port notes: the PR's hunks for cuda.zig/cuda_engine.zig/cuda_forward.zig
#! were hand-adapted to 49a01bb3 (the contexts drifted since the PR's base);
#! the PR's test files stay upstream. cuda.zig gains the dflash_load and taps
#! exports; prefillChunk nulls the taps for chunks ending before the drafter's
#! window; the unpieced tap call takes the new (lo, n) signature.
#! Port-against: 49a01bb3. Owner: the testing line's agent (round 131).
#! Status: under measurement — the tapsqual window (the §2 gates — g2
#! drafted=plain is the correctness gate — + the bench's solo/c2/c4 rows).
